Z||000000||Black88GT||09-15-2000||09:36 PM||||My friend mentioned to me that my 3.4 may be starving for fuel.  I used the 3.4 injectors and I have a new stock fuel pump.  I did not do the adj. fuel regulator due to money issues.  Do you guys think the Holley fuel pump kit would help?  What about that adj. fuel pressure regulator?  Any way I can get better injectors?<P>Also, I have been having this intermittent ticking/clacking coming from the area where the belts are located.  It seemed to be consistent like valve tap, but then it became really inconsistent, almost like popcorn popping mixed with a clacking sound if that makes any sense.  If I am in second gear going like 15 mph, its clacking.  At idle however, its more like a constant tick.<BR>My belts do squeel a little on start up, but it isn't too loud and seems to go away when I start driving.  This may be a coincidence, but I filled the tank half way the other day with 93 octane gas, and thats when it went away.  When my gas started getting low again, thats when it seemed to start back up.  I will refill it tomorrow morning and see if it goes away like last time.  <P><BR>Any ideas??????<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||5
Z||000001||Black88GT||09-16-2000||10:05 PM||||OK the gas had nothing to do with it.  It is obviously coming from the belts or belt area.  <P>come on people, I guess you need to talk about sex in a fiero to get any responses....<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||09-16-2000||10:26 PM||||I have the 3.4 injectors in a 95 Camaro motor in my GT and with the stock fuel pump, stock regulator and chip it runs rich at idle and at full throttle. You would need a chip that leans out the mixture a little at both ends to get more power than what you already have. More fuel is not the answer unless you are going to put more air with it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||09-16-2000||10:28 PM||||Thanks cooter, I wonder if Joe Wynmans chip does that?  I will have to send him an email...||||reg||1
